{% comment %}
  The 1–5 star histogram.

  Rendered in two places — the compact popover under the product title, and
  the full reviews section further down — so it lives in one snippet rather
  than being written twice and drifting.

  Params:
    breakdown   — json map, {"1": n, ... "5": n}
    total       — total rating count, the denominator
    scale_max   — integer, usually 5
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign bd_max = scale_max | default: 5 | floor
  assign bd_total = total | default: 0 | floor
-%}

{%- if breakdown != blank and bd_total > 0 -%}
  <ul class="cited-rating__bars" role="list">
    {%- comment -%}
      Descending, 5 first, because that is the order every shopper has been
      trained to read a ratings histogram in.

      Integer arithmetic throughout: `times: 100` BEFORE `divided_by` keeps
      this exact without ever producing a float, which matters because a float
      reaching a range bound elsewhere in this block raised "invalid integer"
      and silently rendered nothing at all.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for i in (1..bd_max) reversed -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign bucket = i | append: ''
        assign bucket_count = breakdown[bucket] | default: 0 | floor
        assign pct = bucket_count | times: 100 | divided_by: bd_total
      -%}
      <li class="cited-rating__row">
        <span class="cited-rating__row-label">{{ i }} star</span>
        <span class="cited-rating__track">
          <span class="cited-rating__fill" style="width: {{ pct }}%;"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="cited-rating__row-pct">{{ pct }}%</span>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
{%- endif -%}
